EN+=[
 ('sicily','To Sicily','','Alessandro Noto',N,'Yoshi has everything, Jamie carries things he talks to no one about. Two twelve-year-olds meet in a fight on a basketball court and set off for Sicily without their parents, without a plan and with far too little money. A moving coming-of-age novel about friendship, family and the long road to the place you have been dreaming of.'),
 ('catastrophe','The Friendly Catastrophe','A Novel','Konstanze Frey',N,'Michelle Kirstensen can’t keep quiet. When something is wrong and everyone else nods along, she says so, politely, reasonably and with devastating consequences. Then she notices that behind many of her small town’s misfortunes stands the same charming man. A satirical novel about power, going along and civil courage.'),
 ('crown','Crown of Concrete','A Novel','Sandro Urban',N,'Robert grows up in a concrete housing estate on the edge of Hanover with nothing but a notebook full of rhymes. As the rapper Rodeo he climbs to gold records and sold-out arenas, and loses more with every step. A novel about the way up and the harder way back to yourself.'),
 ('maps','Where the Maps End','','Alessandro Noto',N,'Geologist Frank Kern follows an unexplained magnetic anomaly into the Tian Shan mountains of Kazakhstan and wakes up below a city that appears on no map. A novel about home, belief and the price of a single truth.'),
 ('aurora','Project Aurora','Do You Know Who You Are?','Judith Bahlmann',N,'Neuropsychologist Hannah Kordt leads a study on cognitive bias until inconsistencies appear: a wrong date, confidential files, people who know things about her life she never told anyone. A psychological thriller about memory, identity and control.'),
 ('kings','Kings of Ash','A Crime Novel','Evan J. Moore',N,'Milan Bakker grows up in the coal harbor of Novahaven, where the money never stretches far enough. At sixteen he delivers his first backpack, at twenty he meets the man who gives him recognition and access. From bottle collector to money launderer: a dark crime novel about power, money and betrayal.'),
 ('light-shadow','Between Light and Shadow','','Sandro Noto',N,'Emilia, daughter of one of Hamburg’s most influential families, flees an expensive dinner into the rain and meets Adrian in a pub in Hammerbrook. Something begins between them that should not be. Two worlds, one decision.'),
 ('blood-asphalt','Between Blood and Asphalt','A Sky Devils MC Novel','Juna Morel',N,'Roman has been the enforcer of the Sky Devils MC for eight years. Nora fixes engines and asks no questions she doesn’t need answered. When the club heads toward a fateful deal, Roman stands between the family he would sacrifice everything for and the woman who makes him doubt it all. A dark MC romance.'),
 ('jabari','Jabari','A Novel','Amari Diallo',N,'Jabari Omondi is eleven when he promises the rain he will one day buy his mother a real house. From reselling batteries in Kibera and a cramped repair workshop to a scholarship at the University of Nairobi: a novel about education, ambition and the courage to believe in a bigger future.'),
 ('coffee','Coffee','From the Ritual of Sufi Monks to a Global Commodity','Sandro Noto',F,'From a legend about dancing goats in the Ethiopian highlands and the Sufi monks of Yemen to the coffeehouses of the Enlightenment and today’s commodity exchanges: the improbable, contradictory history of the little brown bean in your cup.'),
 ('beer','Beer','From the Song of Ninkasi to Alcohol-Free Beer','Sandro Noto',F,'Nearly four thousand years ago, a Sumerian hymn to the goddess Ninkasi described how to brew beer. In 34 chapters this book follows beer from Mesopotamia and the monastery breweries to the Pilsner revolution, craft beer and alcohol-free beer.'),
 ('shamanism','SHAMANISM','The Big Book of Traditions, Rituals, Power Animals, and the Shamanic Journey','Vivian Dahl',F,'A drumbeat in the night and a world of very different people behind it. In 73 chapters Vivian Dahl travels through the history of shamanism and living traditions around the world, and explains the shamanic worldview, power animals and the shamanic journey.'),
 ('optimized','The Optimized Human','Testosterone, HGH, Peptides, Weight-Loss Injections, and the New Era of Self-Optimization','Viktor Cross',F,'A critical, evidence-oriented history and analysis of human enhancement: from the first doping agents to testosterone, growth hormone, peptides, the GLP-1 revolution, nootropics and longevity protocols.'),
 ('human','What Is a Human Being?','Between Science, Consciousness, and the Question of Reality','Michael Rabenau',F,'Are we a chance product of matter that has become aware of itself, or something more? This book sets out materialism, dualism and idealism as fairly as their best advocates would and tests them against the evidence, from consciousness to free will and quantum physics.'),
 ('invisibility','Learned Invisibility','Why Most People Aren’t Shy, Just Out of Practice','Konstantin Reeder',F,'Most people who feel socially invisible are not shy by nature. Over the years they have learned a behavior that keeps them from standing out. It feels like character, but it is a habit, and habits can be changed.'),
 ('love','Is This Still Love?','A Compass for Women in Difficult Relationships','Friedhelm Westerkamp',F,'“Am I being too sensitive, or is something really wrong here?” This book gives a clear distinction to work with: normal relationship friction, unhealthy but changeable patterns, and toxic or abusive behavior.'),
 ('back-to-life','How I Found My Way Back to Life','An Honest Guide Through Grief, Pain, and the Quiet Return to Yourself','Clara Winter',F,'Not a set of instructions for healing and not a promise that everything will be fine again, but a companion through grief. In seventeen short chapters Clara Winter walks with you through what loss does to you and how it can be carried.'),
 ('fitness','The Big Fitness Book','From Beginner to Pro — Everything for Your Body','Alessandro Noto',F,'Fitness is a question of consistency, knowledge and patience. Training principles, the Big 5 compound lifts, complete plans for every level and the nutrition you need, in one book.'),
 ('gardening','The Big Book of Self-Sufficient Gardening','From Seed to Harvest — Everything for Your Garden','Alessandro Noto',F,'Grow your own vegetables, fruit and herbs, from the first seed to the harvest: soil, sowing, watering and fertilizing, companion planting and crop rotation, plus detailed plant profiles.'),
 ('emigrate','Emigrate, But Where To?','The Honest Compass to 15 Countries – Between Dream and Daily Life','Mika Solberg',F,'Most guides to emigrating say: just take the leap. This book says: look closely first. Fifteen countries compared honestly, with the Emigration Compass to find out which one fits your life fifty weeks a year, not two.'),
]
